Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Dropout Recovery for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: DropoutKiller Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: DropoutKiller Developers <dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Detects technical zero events in single-cell RNA-seq data and
    selectively recovers only selected coordinates. The production detector is
    a source-faithful R port of the scGACL Gamma-Normal mixture detector: raw
    counts are transformed as log(1.01 + count), one mixture is fitted per gene
    within each supplied major cell subpopulation, and observed zeros are called
    from the Gamma-component posterior using the released default threshold of
    0.5. Original ALRA remains available as an explicit comparator using one
    all-cell matrix, ALRA library-size normalization, the original singular-value
    spacing rank heuristic, randomized SVD, and the gene-wise empirical 0.1
    percent low-rank quantile gate. Historical membership-local empirical-Bayes
    and ALRA-quantile detectors remain available for explicit comparison.
    Detection and recovery scales are separated: scGACL uses raw counts while
    recovery can use the ALRA library-size/log working scale. Production recovery
    is the target-safe cross-fitted P1 stabilized state with hierarchy/embedding
    predictor smoothing, positive-donor ridge prediction, predictive uncertainty,
    and exact preservation of observed coordinates on the recovery working scale.
